        "args": {
          "content": "{\n  \"module\": \"multi-page-support\",\n  \"verdict\": \"needs_changes\",\n  \"tool_calls\": 74,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"packages/excalidraw/tests/pages.test.tsx\",\n      \"line\": 342,\n      \"issue\": \"Three defects cause typecheck and test failures in pages.test.tsx: (1) line 342 calls h.store.scheduleCapture(CaptureUpdateAction.IMMEDIATELY) with 1 argument, but Store.scheduleCapture() takes 0 arguments (TS2554); (2) in AC-6 (line 454), exportScene({ type: 'png', config: { embedScene: true } }) calls HTMLCanvasElement.prototype.toBlob which in JSDOM produces an empty non-PNG blob that fails PNG chunk decoding and times out after 5000ms; (3) in AC-7 (line 516), container.querySelector('.search-menu input') returns null because SearchMenu renders its input under `.${CLASSES.SEARCH_MENU_INPUT_WRAPPER} input` (and ListItem calls HTMLElement.prototype.scrollIntoView which is undefined in JSDOM unless mocked).\",\n      \"fix\": \"Call h.store.scheduleCapture() with 0 arguments at line 342; in AC-6, spy on HTMLCanvasElement.prototype.toBlob to pass a valid PNG fixture blob (`const basePng = await API.loadFile('./fixtures/smiley.png')`) before calling exportScene({ type: 'png', ... }) and restore the spy afterward; in AC-7, mock `window.HTMLElement.prototype.scrollIntoView = vi.fn()` and query `.${CLASSES.SEARCH_MENU_INPUT_WRAPPER} input` (importing CLASSES from @excalidraw/common).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"file\": \"packages/excalidraw/scene/export.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1342,\n      \"issue\": \"In exportToBlob, the async callback passed to canvas.toBlob awaits encodePngMetadata without a try/catch block, so any error thrown during PNG metadata encoding results in an unhandled promise rejection and leaves the exportToBlob Promise unsettled forever.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Wrap the PNG embedScene block and resolve(blob) inside canvas.toBlob's async callback in a try { ... } catch (error) { reject(error); } block so errors properly reject the r"
        },
        "canonical_path": null,
        "args_clipped": true
      }
    ]
